    {
      "bbox": [
        161.1343545751634,
        684.9727509469697,
        83.80326307189543,
        16.487241477272732
      ],
      "text": "Weight",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/VGCVEY+CMBX12",
        "size": 14.34619998931885
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        145.61699346405229,
        727.4704027777777,
        758.7950727124183,
        11.449431186868708
      ],
      "text": "In this section, I apply the results presented in Section 3 to an empirical analysis of the distribution of",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/KCENXI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962599754333496
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        120.58823529411765,
        753.2636347853536,
        783.8185216503268,
        11.449444128787889
      ],
      "text": "smoking effects on infant birth weight. Smoking not only has a direct impact on infant birth weight, but is",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/KCENXI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962599754333496
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        120.58823529411765,
        779.0555855429293,
        783.8221058006536,
        11.44944412878786
      ],
      "text": "also associated with unobservable factors that affect infant birth weight. I identify marginal distributions",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/KCENXI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962599754333496
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        120.58823529411765,
        804.8475363005051,
        783.8272140522876,
        11.44944412878786
      ],
      "text": "of potential infant birth weight with and without smoking by making use of a state cigarette tax hike in",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/KCENXI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962599754333496
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        120.58823529411765,
        830.64078125,
        783.8204644607843,
        11.449431186868708
      ],
      "text": "Massachusetts (MA) in January 1993 as a source of exogenous variation. I focus on pregnant women who",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/KCENXI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962599754333496
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        120.58823529411765,
        856.4327320075757,
        783.8152557189542,
        11.449444128787889
      ],
      "text": "change their smoking behavior from smoking to nonsmoking in response to the tax increase. To identify the",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/KCENXI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962599754333496
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        120.58823529411765,
        882.2246827651516,
        783.8304799836601,
        11.449444128787889
      ],
      "text": "distribution of smoking effects, I impose a MTR restriction that smoking has nonpositive effects on infant",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/KCENXI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962599754333496
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        120.58823529411765,
        908.0179238320707,
        255.29829084967318,
        11.449449305555547
      ],
      "text": "birth weight with probability one.",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/KCENXI+CMR10",
        "size": 9.962599754333496
      }
    },
